0.8.1 (2026-08-20)
=====
- Keyboard: introduce unified physical arrow navigation across Search, results, grids, sidebars, Places, and session controls
- Keyboard: route typing and Backspace to Search, improve Calculator and Places focus behavior, and remove Ctrl+Tab focus traversal
- UI: simplify Docked, Centered, and Full Screen composition and Properties controls with adaptive, preset-aware layouts that remain visibly distinct
- UI: redesign Docked and Centered layouts with theme-derived surfaces, dividers, spacing, and responsive control placement
- UI: keep Full Screen's established composition while making Applications/Places placement deterministic
- Presets: substantially refresh Modern, align all built-in presets with the supported layout model, and use Modern by default
- Properties: simplify layout, sidebar, profile, session, and Places settings by removing obsolete options
- Places: present Applications and Places as a flat selector with clearer selection and consistent sizing
- Bugfix: correct horizontal, left, and right sidebar positioning, centering, and relayout behavior
- Bugfix: keep Applications/Places and session controls aligned and consistently sized across layouts
- Bugfix: fix grid sizing, resizing glitches, clipping, and overflow during layout changes and scrolling
- Bugfix: ensure Favorites, Recently Used, and All Applications appear correctly on the first opening
- Bugfix: preserve the configured default page after initial loading
- Bugfix: restore arrow-key navigation after live layout changes and prevent focus regressions
- Installer: prevent the development installer from building the package twice

1.0.0-rc1 (2026-07-29)
=====
- UI: minor Presets and Calculator improvements
- Release: publish verified packages, source archives, and checksums automatically from valid release tags
- Packaging: validate Debian, Ubuntu, Fedora, and Arch package builds, installation, and version ordering
- Packaging: declare required Exo build and runtime helpers across Debian, Fedora, and Arch packages
- Documentation: add the support matrix, known limitations, testing procedures, and translation status
- Community: add security reporting, contribution guidance, and structured issue templates
- Tests: validate dependency declarations, package builds, and legacy/successor Xfce compatibility paths
- Tests: add release identity, artifact contract, documentation, translation, and repository-presentation checks
- Tests: retire obsolete Whisker overlap checks and duplicate release automation
- Bugfix: make edge and corner resizing reliable across presets and display environments
- Bugfix: use the correct Xfce helper APIs across the libxfce4ui 4.21 transition while preserving existing search actions
- Bugifx: "Remember last mode" consistently opens Applications if disabled, if enabled restored Places sessions open on Home.
- Bugfix: Kept Applications and Places controls, search context, and content synchronized across opening, layout, and live setting changes.
- Bugfix: Fixed Transparent grid empty-space clicks leaving stale solid tiles while preserving theme interaction and keyboard-focus feedback.
- Bugfix: Made Places Home shortcuts deterministic by omitting missing, Home-equivalent, and duplicate standard directories.

0.8.0 (2026-07-17)
=====
- Drag and drop: add drag-to-favourite support for applications and Places
- Drag and drop: add desktop drag support for applications, favourites, and Places items
- Drag and drop: keep fullscreen fallback actions available and avoid copying folder contents
- Places: hide stale favourites without modifying external bookmark sources
- Calculator: add optional inline calculation with bc, Qalculate, and GNOME Calculator
- Properties: add Calculator settings for engine, result size, and decimal precision
- Packaging: recommend bc on Debian, Ubuntu, and Fedora while keeping Arch dependencies unchanged
- CI: remove identity-grep job and add calculator tests

0.7.2 (2026-07-13)
